{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BondDecayRates","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BondDecayRates","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.pn_departure_in_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.pn_departure_in_q","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L196-L213","doc":"Its leading coefficient in `δ` is `(q² − 1)/(q² + 1) = tanh(ln q)`: the\ndeparture is `tanh(ln q)·δ + O(δ²)`. Stated as the exact rational form whose\n`δ → 0` limit gives that coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.pn_departure_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.pn_departure_exact","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L188-L194","doc":"The colour-weighted p–n bond's departure from `−1`, exactly. With\n`x = (q + 1/q)/2` and `y = hδ/4`, `|r| = (x − y)/(x + y)` and the departure is\n`2y/(x + y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.tanh_log_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.tanh_log_eq","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L176-L186","doc":"`tanh(ln q) = (q² − 1)/(q² + 1)` for `q > 0`. This is the coefficient that\nturns the colour weight `δ` into the p–n bond's departure from `−1`, and at the\nsubstrate pin it is `0.103963710` — the odd-to-even ratio\n`interaction-sector-taxonomy.md` derives for the electromagnetic coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.like_nucleon_rates_coincide","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.like_nucleon_rates_coincide","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L141-L172","doc":"**WITHDRAWN 2026-09-01.** With the gap correctly magnitude-ordered, `r_pp`\nand `r_nn` are *both* `1/q²`, so the exact relation `r_pp · r_nn = r_pn²` this\nfile previously proved is false as stated (the product is `1/q⁴`, not `1`), and\nthe bar-exchange that carried the strong/weak sector split is vacuous — equal\nrates do not exchange. Recorded as a deletion rather than a restatement: nothing\nreplaces them.\n\nWhat survives is below, and it is the part that did not depend on the ordering:\n`r_pn = 1` exactly for the averaged interface (equal magnitudes either way), and\nits colour-weighted departure carrying `tanh(ln q)`.\n\n**And `like_nucleon_rates_coincide` was empty until 2026-09-03.** The withdrawal\nabove left it stated as\n\n    theorem like_nucleon_rates_coincide {q : ℝ} (_hq : 1 < q) :\n        (1 : ℝ) / q ^ 2 = 1 / q ^ 2 := rfl\n\n— literally `X = X`, closed by `rfl`, with the hypothesis bound under a `_`\nbecause nothing used it. It named the surviving claim and asserted none of it:\n`1/q² = 1/q²` holds for every real `q` and says nothing about nucleon bonds. That\nis the tautological conclusion AGENTS.md §5 bans, and it was found by\n`proof-no-unused-hypothesis-rfl` in the repo's vacuity audit.\n\nIt now states what the name says: that the p–p and n–n rates — reached through\n**different** expressions, `|E₂|/|E₁|` at `d = 0` versus `|E₁|/|E₂|` at\n`d = −h` — are equal. That is falsifiable (the two sides are different terms; the\nordering error this file records made them `1/q²` and `q²`), and the proof\ncomposes `rate_pp` and `rate_nn`, so it genuinely needs `1 < q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.rate_pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.rate_pn","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L124-L137","doc":"**p–n**, strict average (`d = −h/2`): the rate is `−1` **exactly**, for every\n`q`. The averaged interface is the bar-fixed point of the three templates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.rate_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.rate_nn","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L115-L122","doc":"**n–n** (`σ⁻¹`, `d = −h`, `h = q − 1/q`): the rate is `−q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.rate_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.rate_pp","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L106-L113","doc":"**p–p** (`σ`, `d = 0`): the rate is `−1/q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.bondRate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.bondRate","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L92-L104","doc":"The falloff carried across one bond — the transfer step's **spectral gap**,\n`|λ₂/λ₁|` with `λ₁` the LARGER-magnitude eigenvalue.\n\n⚠️ **Corrected 2026-09-01.** This first read `E₂/E₁` in the fixed `(q, −1/q)`\norder, which is the reciprocal of the gap whenever `|E₂| > |E₁|` — as it is for\n`n–n`. `σ⁻¹` has `σ`'s spectrum up to sign, so the gap is `1/q²` for **both**\nlike-nucleon bonds, not `1/q²` and `q²`. Independently derived on `main` by\nbean `qou-brng` (`computations/probes/spectral_gap_bond_decay_probe.py`), which\nhad it right; the two claims this file built on the wrong ordering — an exact\nrelation `r_pp·r_nn = r_pn²` and a bar-exchange giving a strong/weak sector\nsplit — are **withdrawn**, not restated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.transferE2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.transferE2","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L89-L90","doc":"`E₂` of the same step: the `σ`-eigenvalue `−1/q` shifted by `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.transferE1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.transferE1","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BondDecayRates.lean#L85-L87","doc":"`E₁` of a one-letter transfer step with offset `d`: the `σ`-eigenvalue `q`\nshifted by `d`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}